{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_145214343#8_316451218","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to plutonium-239 and its uses, and directly explains that Pu-239 is used in nuclear power reactors, generates electricity, contributes substantially to commercial nuclear plant energy, and can be added to fuel to make MOX fuel.","learned":"Plutonium-239 improves energy technology by serving as a fissile fuel in nuclear reactors and MOX fuel, producing large amounts of electricity."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q977","reason":"This plutonium uses/applications query produced a strong grade-3 result on energy technology; continue for more direct application-overview evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q977"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_90922177#1_170513191","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q977","rank":2,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_90922177#1_170513191\" , \"end_char\": 962.000000 , \"headings\": \"Flux Capacitor Flux Capacitor Details Product Information Applications for this Product Detailed Description \" , \"segment\": \"<cover>Plutonium Working Speed (mph): 88 Maximum Power: 121 Gigawatts Applications </cover>for this Product Modifications: Time Travel Quantity: 1 Detailed Description Time Travel at your own RISK! Plutonium is required to properly operate the flux  capacitor Plutonium is used by the onboard nuclear reactor  which then powers the flux capacitor to provide  the needed 1.21 gigawatts of electrical power. Plutonium not available and O'Reilly Auto  Parts. Please contact your local plutonium  supplier. Flux capacitor requires the stainless steel body of  a 1981-1983 DeLorean DMC-12 to properly function. Once the time machine travels at 88 mph (142  km/h), light coming from the flux capacitor  pulses until it becomes a steady stream of light  at which point time travel begins!\" , \"start_char\": 196.000000 , \"title\": \"Flux Capacitor - Great Scott! | O'Reilly Auto Parts\" ,"}}
